
- Affected when the player is moving, traveling, changing location, or navigating terrain.
  Short movements (30 feet, crossing a room, climbing a wall) still count if they
  matter mechanically (e.g. provoking opportunity attacks, difficult terrain).
- Affected when the action is about proximity to specific world elements: approaching
  or moving toward NPCs, creatures, objects, or landmarks (e.g. a lake, a door, a
  tree, the goblins). "I approach the goblins", "I move toward the lake", "I get
  closer to the altar" all affect traversal because they change the character's
  position relative to those elements.
- destination: the name of the target location from the STORY LOCATIONS above, if any.
  Match the player's words to the closest location name. Set to null if the target
  is an entity or landmark rather than a named story location.
